        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: be6b611a6ce3af30cfad1166d418ae98034301b63423515ba5bf0b069a79f313\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 6ea04e54af46122495d50fe5810cf2021e5eec12b22c3b4bcad667d91dfc54c9\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Prune VLAN 1 from any trunk links as necessary:\n\nSW1(config)#int g0/2\nSW1(config-if)#switchport trunk allowed vlan except 1\n\nVerify that VLAN 1 is not allowed on the trunk link:\n\nSW1#show interfaces trunk\n\nPort Mode Encapsulation Status Native vlan\nGi0/1 on 802.1q trunking 1\nGi0/2 on 802.1q trunking 1\n\nPort Vlans allowed on trunk\nGi0/1 1-998,1000-4094\nGi0/2 2-4094",
          "group_id": "V-220643",
          "group_id_src": "V-220643",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000009",
          "rule_id": "SV-220643r991850_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220643r991850_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have the default VLAN pruned from all trunk ports that do not require it.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000230",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "80559ebc-efb2-517c-a1bb-28d2f87b30c7",
          "uuid": "2a8f7d4b-746b-5c48-aaa5-698ddfe7a458",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: be6b611a6ce3af30cfad1166d418ae98034301b63423515ba5bf0b069a79f313\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 6ea04e54af46122495d50fe5810cf2021e5eec12b22c3b4bcad667d91dfc54c9\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the switch for management access to use a VLAN other than the default VLAN:\n\nSW1(config)#int vlan 22\nSW1(config-if)#ip add 10.1.22.3 255.255.255.0\nSW1(config-if)#no shut",
          "group_id": "V-220644",
          "group_id_src": "V-220644",
