          "uuid": "d30d65f1-f361-57dc-9bc8-832e0b15592f",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: be6b611a6ce3af30cfad1166d418ae98034301b63423515ba5bf0b069a79f313\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 6ea04e54af46122495d50fe5810cf2021e5eec12b22c3b4bcad667d91dfc54c9\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Disable trunking on all user-facing or untrusted switch ports:\n\nSW1(config)#int g0/6\nSW1(config-if)#switchport mode access\nSW1(config-if)#end",
          "group_id": "V-220645",
          "group_id_src": "V-220645",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000011",
          "rule_id": "SV-220645r991853_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-220645r991853_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must have all user-facing or untrusted ports configured as access switch ports.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-L2-000250",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "80559ebc-efb2-517c-a1bb-28d2f87b30c7",
          "uuid": "d2107190-b2b2-5ddd-b768-edbaaf0c42c3",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: be6b611a6ce3af30cfad1166d418ae98034301b63423515ba5bf0b069a79f313\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: 6ea04e54af46122495d50fe5810cf2021e5eec12b22c3b4bcad667d91dfc54c9\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "To ensure the integrity of the trunk link and prevent unauthorized access, the ID of the native VLAN of the trunk port must be changed from the default VLAN (i.e., VLAN 1) to its own unique VLAN ID. \n\nSW1(config)#int g0/1\nSW1(config-if)#switchport trunk native vlan 44\n\nNote: The native VLAN ID must be the same on both ends of the trunk link; otherwise, traffic could accidentally leak between broadcast domains.",
          "group_id": "V-220646",
          "group_id_src": "V-220646",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000512-L2S-000012",
          "rule_id": "SV-220646r991854_rule",
